{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791128929,"nonce":"eeOUzB+AuG+gQV1IbZOt17Qh/u4=","title":"Host schema: native bindings so plugin calls and fields are direct","message":"Caribou 0a1ced7 \"one native boundary\". Measured by caribou (Python calling a do-nothing caribou_abi math plugin through host imports, 1M-iteration loops): loop alone 4.4 ns; Math.hypot(f64, f64) on the keyed float path 120 ns; Math.twice(i32) on the generic path 306 ns. The cost is the chain $Foreign$invoke -\u003e dyn Foreign -\u003e by-name dispatch -\u003e caribou bridge -\u003e plugin thunk. Goal: plugin members as cheap as a ZRTL symbol call, plugin fields as cheap as a Zyntax field.\n\nAgreed design (with caribou):\n1. HostMethod gains native: Option\u003cNativeBinding\u003e, HostField native: Option\u003cNativeField\u003e. A binding names a symbol the embedder registers (register_function_typed), so a call lowers to an ordinary Import in every tier, typed operands, no box, no member-name string. Lowered in zyntax_embed host_import (ZynML) and in zyntax_python's typed host path (host_method / host_attribute).\n2. Natively bound classes are held as the raw core word (i64 handle), not a foreign box. Receiver pass: Indirect(8): a plugin object is { *const TypeDesc, payload: *mut c_void }, so the receiver is one load of word+8.\n3. NativeField {offset, kind}: p.x / p.x = v lower to a load/store at payload + offset, no call. Caribou adds declared fields to plugin! (FieldDesc: name, offset_of!, tag; ABI bump).\n4. Operand kinds: i/u/f widths, bool, void, opaque word, borrowed str (data = s + 16, len from the header; two operands), borrowed bytes/buffers (ptr, len), core enum as opaque, and object-of-class-C carrying C's binding (a typed word). String results come back as a core string converted by a caribou-registered symbol $Host$text_to_string (one copy).\n5. Errors: may_raise members are followed by a load of a per-thread pending byte and a not-taken branch; the byte's address comes from $Host$pending_flag() called once per frame that has a may_raise call; the slow path takes the error. NOTHROW members skip the check.\n6. ZRTL stays Zyntax's std; user plugins use caribou_abi; the binding is the shared fast path.\n\nMeasure: Python and ZynML to plugin, call / field / string rows, against the numbers above.","files":null}]}